# Circutor CEM M-RS485.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Circutor CEM M-RS485 — Optical-to-RS485 Modbus Bridge for CEM Energy Meters
# | 
# | Source: circutor-cem-m-rs485-communications-manual.pdf (section 4.4, pp. 12-18)
# | Device: DIN-rail module that couples to the optical service port of CEM C10/C20/C30 meters,
# | exposing their measurement data via RS-485 Modbus RTU.
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU, FC03/04 read, FC10 write, 8N1 default
# | Baud: 9600/19200/38400 bps (configurable at 0x03E9 = 1001)
# | Register availability varies by coupled meter (C10 / C20 / C30); see Table 11 in source.
# | All 32-bit values occupy 2 consecutive registers; addresses shown in decimal (source is hex).
# | Scaling: voltage ×10 (1 decimal), current ×100 (2 decimals), cos φ ×100 (2 decimals).
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Circutor
@model=CEM M-RS485
@vendor_website=circutor.com
@description=Optical-to-RS485 Modbus bridge for CEM C10/C20/C30 energy meters. Exposes CEM meter via FC03/04 (read) and FC10 (write). Energy u32 Wh/varh at addr 0-58; instantaneous s32 at 1842-1884 (V×10, A×100, cos φ×100, W/var/VA). Config at 1000-1002. Same register map as CEM-C31.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/circutor-cem-m-rs485.toml; Source: circutor-cem-m-rs485-communications-manual.pdf (section 4.4, pp. 12-18). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

